NkMail mailio security/read-only compatibility patch
Upstream: mailio tag 0.26.1
Base-commit: f358b1f85f9a021f0bd814e285eb8ae102fc8f79
Apply from third_party/mailio with: patch -p1 < ../../patches/mailio/0001-verified-tls-peek-timeouts.patch

Purpose:
- Per-connection Asio context, asynchronous DNS/connect/TLS, cancellation-safe
  nonzero per-I/O deadlines (not a whole-operation deadline).
- System trust roots plus optional ca_file, mandatory verify_peer, DNS/IP
  hostname verification, DNS SNI, TLS >= 1.2. No plaintext fallback.
- Add opt-in FETCH PEEK without changing existing FETCH overload behavior;
  parse BODY sections and UID appearing after FLAGS/body; bound literals.
- Fix empty quoted atoms, instance-local literal counters, and selectable
  folder metadata so hierarchy parents marked Noselect are not opened.
- Explicit SMTP 4xx/5xx rejection bit and strict final DATA status parsing;
  malformed/transport failures during submission stay Unknown in adapter.
- SMTP upstream already envelopes To/Cc/Bcc while message.format defaults
  add_bcc_header=false; adapter/fixture verify Bcc never appears in DATA.

Verification: independent Qt C++ probe plus Python loopback IMAP/SMTP/TLS
fixture. No real credentials, external connections, mailbox writes or sends.
30 scenarios passed including expired/untrusted/wrong-host certificates for
both TLS modes/protocols, PEEK/header pagination/UIDVALIDITY, Chinese MIME,
binary attachments, Bcc privacy, refusal/ambiguous disconnect and TLS timeout.

Limits: folders currently requests STATUS serially for each selectable folder;
headers are capped at 256 KiB each, full MIME at 25 MiB, attachments 15 MiB each.
The adapter enforces post-parse MIME tree depth/part bounds; this is not a full
upstream hostile-MIME parser audit. Timeout applies to individual I/O only.

